    <h2 style="margin-top:0">The discount, in plain numbers</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Monthly plan:</strong> $150/month instead of $175/month. $0 down. Discount applies for the entire duration of the engagement &mdash; not just the first year. <strong>That is $300/year saved, every year you stay.</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Lump-sum plan:</strong> $3,500 instead of $4,000 for a full custom-coded site, ownership transferred to you on launch.</li>
      <li><strong>Free 5-point audit either way.</strong> If you are not ready to build yet, the <a href="/audit/" class="inline-link">free audit</a> is also free, and I will mark you flagged for the discount the day you do hire me.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who qualifies</h2>
    <p>Any licensed medical, dental, allied-health, or mental-health professional in active practice or licensed retirement, plus their immediate family:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Physicians.</strong> MDs, DOs, residents, fellows.</li>
      <li><strong>Dental.</strong> DDS / DMD, dental hygienists, oral surgeons, orthodontists, endodontists, periodontists, prosthodontists.</li>
      <li><strong>Nursing.</strong> RNs, LPNs / LVNs, NPs, CRNAs, midwives, nursing assistants.</li>
      <li><strong>Allied health.</strong> PAs, physical therapists, occupational therapists, speech-language pathologists, audiologists, respiratory therapists, optometrists, opticians, podiatrists, chiropractors, registered dietitians, pharmacists.</li>
      <li><strong>Mental health.</strong> Licensed psychologists, LCSWs / LMFTs / LPCs / LMHCs, board-certified psychiatrists, board-certified behavior analysts.</li>
      <li><strong>Medical imaging and lab.</strong> Radiologic technologists, sonographers, medical lab scientists, phlebotomists with state licensure.</li>
      <li><strong>Spouses, children, parents, and siblings</strong> of any qualifying clinician &mdash; same discount, same verification (one shared photo of the clinician's license, plus a one-line note identifying the relationship).</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>How verification works:</strong> One photo or scan of your active license &mdash; state board card, hospital ID with clinical role visible, or a current verification printout from your state licensing board. Email it once when we start; I delete the file the moment I confirm. I do not retain copies of your documents.</p>

    <h2>How to claim it</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Book a 20-minute discovery call.</strong> <a href="/contact/" class="inline-link">Standard contact form</a>. In the message, mention you are claiming the medical personnel discount.</li>
      <li><strong>On the call, we figure out the build.</strong> Same conversation I have with anyone &mdash; what your practice needs, which plan fits, which features matter. (If you are HIPAA-touching with intake forms, I will walk you through the appropriate intake-form provider; I do not handle PHI directly.)</li>
      <li><strong>Send proof of license.</strong> One photo of your license card or a current state-board verification, by email. Takes 30 seconds.</li>
      <li><strong>I apply the discount on day one.</strong> Your first invoice is at the discounted rate, not the standard rate. There is no "ramp" or "after first year" reset.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>A note on HIPAA and intake forms</h2>
    <p>I build the marketing site &mdash; pages, blog, service descriptions, hours, location. <strong>I do not store or process PHI on the website.</strong> Patient intake, scheduling, and any form that collects personal health information goes through a HIPAA-compliant third-party provider (Jotform HIPAA, Tebra, SimplePractice, Healee, etc., depending on your specialty). Your site links to and embeds those forms; the data does not pass through my servers. We will set this up correctly during the build.</p>

    <h2>Why I do this</h2>
    <p>A meaningful number of clinicians are launching independent or part-time private practice as the healthcare landscape shifts. The licensing and credentialing burden is enormous, the schedule is brutal, and the work has real human stakes. If a $25/month or $500 lump-sum gap is the difference between having a real website and not, that is a gap worth closing.</p>

